      "period": "classical",
      "gloss": "colour, brown (in the oven or the sun)",
      "evidence": [
        "Cato Agr. 80: <span lang=\"la\">item unguitō colōrātōque caldum nē nimium</span>",
        "Cic. de Or. 2.60: <span lang=\"la\">cum in sōle ambulem, nātūrā fit ut colōrer</span> (Lewis &amp; Short)"
      ],
      "comment": "Lewis &amp; Short: “to colour reddish or brownish”, of a man walking in the sun or pears ripening. Cato uses it of his fried honey-cakes, which are to be browned, “not too much”."
